return [
    '/office-furniture/' => 'Office furniture is the backbone of any productive workspace, and the right pieces keep staff comfortable, organised and focused through a long Lagos working day. This section brings together everything OfficeLand supplies to furnish a business, school or government office end to end: desks and tables, seating of every grade, partitions and screens, and storage from filing cabinets to lockers. Think of it as the starting point for planning a floor rather than buying one item at a time. When you are furnishing or refurbishing, work from how each area is used. Reception and boardrooms carry your brand and need to impress; open-plan floors need durable, repeatable workstations and task chairs; records rooms need secure, fire-resistant storage. Build quality matters in Nigeria, where humidity, dust and heavy daily use test cheap materials quickly, so favour sealed laminates, powder-coated steel and reputable mechanisms backed by a clear warranty. OfficeLand carries a broad range of office furniture in Lagos and delivers nationwide, with professional installation and space planning for complete fit-outs. We handle bulk orders, tenders and phased rollouts for schools, ministries and corporate headquarters. Browse the subcategories below, then request a quote and our team will respond within four working hours.',

    '/office-furniture/desks-tables/' => 'Desks and tables set the rhythm of a workspace, defining where people concentrate, meet and welcome visitors. This category spans executive desks for directors, open-plan workstations for teams, conference tables for the boardroom, reception desks for your front of house and height-adjustable desks for staff who alternate between sitting and standing. Choosing well starts with measuring the room and mapping circulation so that chairs can pull out, walkways stay clear and the space does not feel cramped. Standard working-desk height sits around 720 to 750 millimetres, with depth enough to hold a monitor at arm\'s length. For Nigerian offices, surface material is a practical decision as much as an aesthetic one: thick melamine or HPL laminate over engineered board resists scratches, heat and humidity far better than thin veneers, while powder-coated steel frames and solid-wood edges survive years of knocks. Check cable management, edge banding and the warranty before you commit. OfficeLand stocks office desks and tables in Lagos across many finishes and sizes, and we deliver and professionally install throughout Nigeria. Whether you need a single executive desk or a matched set of workstations for a new floor, request a quote and we will respond within four working hours.',

    '/office-furniture/desks-tables/conference-tables/' => 'A conference table is where decisions get made, so it needs to seat everyone comfortably, carry power and data cleanly, and project the right impression to clients and partners. OfficeLand supplies boardroom and conference tables in Lagos in boat-shaped, rectangular, oval and modular configurations, from compact six-seaters for a meeting room to long directors\' tables for a formal boardroom. Size the table to the room first: allow roughly 600 millimetres of width per person and at least a metre of clearance all around for chairs and movement, then confirm the top can take that length without sagging. For connected meetings, look for built-in cable ports, flip-top power modules and discreet routing so laptops and screens stay tidy. Material choice drives both looks and longevity. Thick laminate and veneer tops over sturdy engineered cores hold up to daily use and Lagos humidity better than delicate finishes, and heavy pedestal or panel legs keep a long table stable. Modular tables that split into smaller units suit training rooms and multipurpose halls. OfficeLand delivers and installs conference tables nationwide and handles full boardroom fit-outs for corporates, ministries and institutions. Tell us your room dimensions and seating target and request a quote; we respond within four working hours.',

    '/office-furniture/desks-tables/executive-desks/' => 'An executive desk anchors a director\'s or manager\'s office and signals seniority, so it should combine a commanding presence with real working practicality. OfficeLand offers executive desks in Lagos in a range of styles, from classic dark-wood finishes for traditional corner offices to sleek contemporary designs with clean lines, usually paired with a return or side credenza for extra surface and storage. When choosing, balance scale against the room so the desk fills the space without overwhelming it; a generous top gives room for a monitor, documents and a visitor\'s paperwork, while an attached pedestal keeps files and valuables within reach. Build quality is where executive desks earn their keep. Look for thick laminate or genuine veneer over a solid engineered core, properly banded edges, soft-close drawer runners and a lockable drawer for confidential papers, all of which cope well with Nigeria\'s humidity and years of daily use. Integrated cable management keeps the setup clean for executives who run multiple devices. OfficeLand delivers and professionally installs executive desks throughout Nigeria and can match a desk with executive seating and storage for a coordinated office. For a single statement desk or a suite of director offices, request a quote and we will respond within four working hours.',

    '/office-furniture/desks-tables/height-adjustable-desks/' => 'Height-adjustable and sit-stand desks let staff move between sitting and standing through the day, easing back strain and keeping energy up during long shifts. OfficeLand supplies height-adjustable desks in Lagos in both electric and manual crank versions, as single workstations and in bench configurations for teams. Electric models raise and lower at the touch of a button and often store preset heights for shared desks, while manual and pneumatic options are simpler and need no power supply, which suits sites where mains stability is a concern. When choosing, check the height range fits both shorter and taller users, confirm the lifting capacity comfortably carries monitors, a dock and accessories, and look for a stable frame that does not wobble at full extension. A smooth, quiet motor and a solid warranty on the mechanism are worth paying for, since the moving parts are what a cheap desk gets wrong. For Nigerian offices, a sturdy steel frame with a scratch-resistant laminate top handles humidity and constant adjustment well. OfficeLand delivers and installs sit-stand desks nationwide and can equip a whole floor for a wellbeing-focused fit-out. Tell us how many positions you need and request a quote; our team responds within four working hours.',

    '/office-furniture/desks-tables/reception-desks/' => 'The reception desk is the first thing visitors see, so it has to look polished while giving your front-desk staff a practical place to work. OfficeLand supplies reception and front-desk counters in Lagos in straight, L-shaped and curved designs, with raised transaction tops that screen the working surface and keep paperwork and monitors out of a visitor\'s eyeline. Choose a size and shape that suits your lobby and foot traffic: a single receptionist needs a different footprint from a busy counter handling queues, and the desk should leave clear space for wheelchair access and a comfortable standing height for guests. Think about the receptionist\'s side too, with room for a chair, a drawer unit, cable routing for phone and computer, and a lockable pedestal for valuables. Material and finish carry your brand, so durable laminates, acrylic or glass accents and optional illuminated logo panels all work well, and sealed surfaces resist the marks and humidity of a Lagos lobby. OfficeLand delivers and professionally installs reception desks across Nigeria and can match them with visitor seating for a complete front-of-house. To specify a counter that fits your space and branding, request a quote and we will respond within four working hours.',

