    '/office-furniture/partitions-screens/' => 'Partitions and screens divide an open floor into usable, focused areas without the cost and permanence of building walls, and they help manage noise, privacy and the flow of people. OfficeLand supplies office partitions and desk screens in Lagos in several forms: floor-standing and demountable partition systems for creating meeting rooms and private offices, desk-mounted screens that separate workstations, and freestanding movable panels for flexible layouts. Choosing the right type depends on what you need the division to do. For meeting rooms, glazed or part-glazed partitions keep light flowing while containing conversation; for open-plan desks, fabric-covered acoustic screens absorb sound and can double as pinboards; for spaces that change often, mobile screens on castors let you reconfigure in minutes. Consider height carefully, since a screen that gives seated privacy differs from one that fully encloses a room. For Nigerian offices, look for sturdy aluminium or steel framing, wipe-clean fabric or laminate surfaces and glazing with proper safety standards, all of which withstand humidity and daily handling. OfficeLand delivers and professionally installs partition systems across Nigeria and plans complete space divisions for growing teams and new fit-outs. Describe the areas you want to create and request a quote; we respond within four working hours.',

    '/office-furniture/seating/' => 'Seating is the single most important investment in staff comfort and health, because people spend most of the working day in a chair, and the wrong one shows up quickly in aches, fatigue and complaints. This category covers every grade OfficeLand supplies: ergonomic and task chairs for daily desk work, executive chairs for senior offices, conference chairs for the boardroom, visitor and reception chairs for waiting areas, and recliner and lounge chairs for breakout spaces. The right choice depends on how long someone sits and what they do. Full-day desk users need adjustable, supportive ergonomic seating; occasional meeting or visitor seating can prioritise style and stacking over heavy adjustment. Whatever the grade, build quality decides how long a chair lasts, so look for sturdy bases, quality gas lifts, breathable mesh or hard-wearing fabric and a clear warranty on the mechanism. In Nigeria\'s warm climate, breathable backrests and durable upholstery that resists wear make a real difference to comfort and lifespan. OfficeLand stocks office chairs in Lagos across all these grades and delivers nationwide, with professional installation for bulk orders. Whether you are replacing a few chairs or seating an entire floor, explore the subcategories below and request a quote; our team responds within four working hours.',

